# Copy to .env and fill in. The app runs on bundled mock data if these are absent.
#
# ZERO secrets of any kind belong in this file — it is bundled into the app and
# is readable by anyone who downloads the .ipa. The Supabase anon key is the
# sole exception, and only because it is designed to be public: it grants
# nothing on its own, because every table enforces row-level security.
#
# There are no news-API keys anywhere in Bite any more (Phase 15.1 removed the
# last one), and no Edge Function secret has lived here since the guardian-body
# proxy was deleted. Every remaining function is server-invoked and keeps its
# own server-only secret in supabase/functions/.env.secrets — see migration
# 0026 for the rotation procedure. Do not reintroduce one here.

# Supabase project (Settings → API in the dashboard). Persistence is skipped
# when these are absent — the app falls back to in-memory state.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
